description:
after being idle for some time >10s
if i rotate the voltage knob once or press the voltage knob i enter the edit mode 
when pressing the voltage knob in editing mode the digit moves left once and moves back to the right most digit if its all the way left already
during the edit mode the editing digit blinks with about 1Hz 
the target voltage is displayed then if i rotate once right after that the editing digit changes by one if i rotate twice it changes by two  
if i wait for about 2s the digit stops blinking if i rotate then once the digit starts blinking again if i rotate twice instead the digit starts blinking and changes by one only
after about 9s the editing mode ends fully and the editing digit resets to the middle right digit when i reenter the editing mode

in editing mode and if the output is off the target voltage/current can be read via spi if the ouput is on and the device is not in editing mode the voltage/current is the actual voltage/current
editing mode timings of voltage/current might be independent or might not be test that too

i dont know about the current timings havent tested it before but the timings might be different 


add a function that is for a full re calibration
it retests all configuration even the pin mapping of the rotators or buttons might be different (try all combinations and check if a change happens)
also tests the timings like the delay needed between two rotations and two button pressed and the ~2s and the ~9s delays for the changes of the editing mode 
get the time by doing binary search around the expected delay 
eg for the 2s delay 
    enter editing mode by waiting then rotating/pressing once 
    try if rotating once after the binary search delay changes the digit or if it does not 
    the time for it to no longer change is the actual time 

the results of the calibration should be saved in flash and queryable/setable via scpi for manual changes


the 2s or the 9s might be multiples of the button scan time of about 10ms or the 50ms of display update those can be counted with the spi handler 
every about 10ms the supply scans for button presses via the spi lines and every like 50ms it updates the display data

